  "title": "Group the Anagrams",
  "category": "Strings",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "description": "<p>Given a list of words, group together the words that are anagrams of each other (same letters, possibly in a different order).</p><p>Inside each group, sort the words lexicographically (identical words are kept, each occurrence counts). Then print the groups ordered by their first (smallest) word.</p><pre>Input:\n6\neat tea tan ate nat bat\n\nOutput:\nate eat tea\nbat\nnat tan</pre><h4>Constraints</h4><ul><li>1 &le; n &le; 1000</li><li>Each word has 1 to 10 lowercase letters</li></ul><h4>Input</h4><ul><li>Line 1: an integer <code>n</code></li><li>Line 2: <code>n</code> words separated by single spaces</li></ul><h4>Output</h4><p>One group per line, the words of a group separated by single spaces.</p>",
  "solution": "n = int(input())\nwords = input().split()\ng = {}\nfor w in words:\n    g.setdefault(''.join(sorted(w)), []).append(w)\ngroups = sorted(sorted(v) for v in g.values())\nfor v in groups:\n    print(' '.join(v))\n",
