  "description": "<p>You start at index <code>0</code>. From index <code>i</code> you may jump forward by any distance from <code>1</code> to <code>a[i]</code>. Find the minimum number of jumps needed to reach the last index.</p><p><b>Constraints:</b></p><ul><li><code>1 &le; N &le; 3000</code></li><li><code>0 &le; a[i] &le; 1000</code></li></ul><h4>Input</h4><p>The first line contains an integer <code>N</code>. The second line contains <code>N</code> space-separated integers.</p><h4>Output</h4><p>Print the minimum number of jumps, or <code>-1</code> if the last index cannot be reached. If <code>N = 1</code> the answer is <code>0</code>.</p>",
  "solution": "n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\njumps = end = far = 0\nans = 0\nfor i in range(n - 1):\n    if i > far:\n        break\n    far = max(far, i + a[i])\n    if i == end:\n        jumps += 1\n        end = far\n        if end >= n - 1:\n            break\nprint(jumps if far >= n - 1 or n == 1 else -1)\n",
