  "id": "o04",
  "title": "Koko Eating Bananas",
  "category": "Sorting & Searching",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "description": "<p>Koko has <code>n</code> piles of bananas and <code>h</code> hours. Each hour she picks one pile and eats <code>k</code> bananas from it; if the pile has fewer than <code>k</code> bananas she eats them all and does nothing else that hour. Find the <b>minimum integer speed</b> <code>k</code> that lets her finish all piles within <code>h</code> hours. Binary search on the answer.</p><ul><li>1 &le; n &le; 2000, n &le; h &le; 10<sup>9</sup></li><li>1 &le; pile &le; 10<sup>9</sup></li></ul><h4>Input</h4><p>Line 1: <code>n h</code>. Line 2: <code>n</code> pile sizes.</p><h4>Output</h4><p>The minimum speed <code>k</code>.</p><h4>Example</h4><p>Input:</p><pre>4 8\n3 6 7 11</pre><p>Output:</p><pre>4</pre>",
  "solution": "n, h = map(int, input().split())\np = list(map(int, input().split()))\nlo, hi = 1, max(p)\nwhile lo < hi:\n    m = (lo + hi) // 2\n    if sum((x + m - 1) // m for x in p) <= h:\n        hi = m\n    else:\n        lo = m + 1\nprint(lo)\n",
