  "description": "<p>Each child <code>i</code> has a greed factor <code>g[i]</code>: the minimum cookie size that will content them. Each cookie <code>j</code> has a size <code>s[j]</code>. Each child gets at most one cookie and each cookie goes to at most one child. Print the <b>maximum number of content children</b>.</p><ul><li>1 &le; number of children, cookies &le; 3000</li><li>1 &le; g[i], s[j] &le; 10<sup>6</sup></li></ul><h4>Input</h4><p>Line 1: number of children. Line 2: greed factors. Line 3: number of cookies. Line 4: cookie sizes.</p><h4>Output</h4><p>The maximum number of content children.</p><h4>Example</h4><p>Input:</p><pre>3\n1 2 3\n2\n1 1</pre><p>Output:</p><pre>1</pre>",
  "solution": "input()\ng = sorted(map(int, input().split()))\ninput()\ns = sorted(map(int, input().split()))\ni = 0\nfor x in s:\n    if i < len(g) and x >= g[i]:\n        i += 1\nprint(i)\n",
